---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — World Cup Draft Simulator"
  description="Privacy policy for World Cup Draft Simulator. Explains what data is collected when you use the fantasy football draft simulator website."
>

<main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase">
      Legal
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl">
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-secondary">Last updated: 2026</p>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      World Cup Draft Simulator is a free browser soccer game and fantasy
      soccer world cup draft simulator. This Privacy Policy explains, in plain
      language, what information we collect when you visit and use the site, how
      that information is used, and the choices you have. It applies to the
      soccer simulator, the football draft simulator, and every page of the
      world cup fantasy game, including the teams index, the how-to-play guide
      and the draft tool itself. Because the app runs entirely in your browser
      with no account and no download, the amount of data involved is small,
      and this policy is written to reflect that. We believe a world cup
      simulator should be as private as it is fun, so we have kept the
      explanation short where we can and detailed where it matters. By using the
      site you agree to the practices described below, and if anything is
      unclear you can reach us through the contact page.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">1. Overview</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          World Cup Draft Simulator ("we", "us", "our") respects your privacy
          and this Privacy Policy is where we explain how. The policy covers the
          entire fantasy football world cup experience — the soccer simulator
          you play in the browser, the football draft simulator that builds your
          XI, the teams index you scout, and the how-to-play guide you read — and
          it describes what information is collected when you visit and use this
          website, how it is used, and the controls available to you. We are a
          free browser soccer game with no subscription and no account, which
          means the relationship is simple: you open the online soccer game, you
          play, and we collect only what we need to keep it running smoothly. By
          using the site you agree to the practices described here, and if those
          practices change we will post the update on this page with a new "Last
          updated" date. This policy is not a contract that grants you rights
          beyond what the law provides, but it is our genuine commitment to treat
          your visit to this interactive soccer simulator with care. Where local
          law gives you stronger protection — for example under GDPR in the EU or
          similar rules elsewhere — that stronger protection applies, and this
          policy is written to sit within it rather than override it. We have
          also designed the app so that a world cup fantasy game respects the
          people who play it: collection is minimised, selling data does not
          happen, and you can clear everything with a couple of clicks. If you
          ever want the shortest version, it is this: we built a soccer game no
          download so you could play between matches, and we intend to keep your
          visit as private as the game is free.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">2. Information we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This is a browser-based game, and that shapes what we collect. We do
          not require an account, and we do not collect personal information
          such as your name, email address or payment details to play, because
          the world cup simulator has no sign-up and no purchases. The game
          state — your draft, your squad, your formation choices, your
          tournament results and your saved cups — is stored only in your own
          browser using local storage, and it is not sent to our servers. That
          means the soccer simulator you enjoy is, by design, a private activity
          that lives on your device; closing the tab or clearing storage removes
          it. In addition to that local state, we may collect standard,
          non-identifying technical data such as your IP address, browser type,
          device type, operating system, the pages you visited and the time
          spent on them, so we can understand how the football draft simulator
          is used and improve the experience. This technical data is aggregated
          and does not, on its own, tell us who you are. We do not use it to
          build a profile of your real identity, and we do not combine it with
          the rosters you draft. Because the app is a free browser soccer game
          with no download, the only things that leave your device are routine
          analytics hits that help us see which features — drafting, the knockout
          bracket, the penalty shootout simulator — players actually use. If you
          prefer not to share even that, you can disable analytics cookies in
          your browser settings and the interactive soccer simulator will still
          work, because every match is computed on your machine rather than on
          our servers. In short, the information we collect is limited to what
          keeps the fantasy soccer draft running and helps us make it better.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">3. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may use cookies and similar technologies to remember preferences
          and to collect analytics about site usage. Third-party analytics
          providers may use cookies to measure traffic and trends, such as how
          many people open the soccer simulator, which football formations are
          drafted most, and whether the teams index is useful before a match.
          These cookies are not required to play — the world cup simulation runs
          entirely on your device — but they help us decide what to improve next.
          You can disable cookies in your browser settings at any time, and the
          browser soccer game will continue to function; the only loss is the
          anonymous usage signal we use to prioritise work. We do not use
          advertising cookies, and we do not run third-party ad networks on this
          fantasy soccer draft site, so there is no cross-site tracking built
          into the experience. If you came to us as a soccer draft game, a free
          soccer simulation game or an interactive soccer simulator, you can
          expect a clean, ad-light environment where cookies are limited to
          basic analytics and preference memory. Some browsers also offer
          "Do Not Track" signals; where we can honour them without breaking the
          online soccer game, we do. Because this is a soccer game no download,
          there is no installed software phoning home in the background — the
          only network activity is the page load and, if enabled, anonymised
          analytics. We review our cookie use regularly and remove anything that
          is no longer needed, keeping the world cup fantasy game as light and
          respectful of your settings as the day it launched.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">4. How we use information</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Information we collect is used to operate, maintain and improve the
          site, to understand how visitors use the game, and to fix bugs and
          performance issues. Concretely, that means making the soccer simulator
          faster, checking that every football formation drafts correctly, and
          confirming the penalty shootout simulator resolves fairly on the
          devices players actually use. We look at aggregated trends — not
          individual drafts — to decide which historical squads to add next and
          whether the world cup simulation feels balanced across eras. We do not
          sell your personal information, and we do not rent it or share it for
          advertising. The fantasy soccer draft you build stays on your device,
          and the only data that reaches us is the anonymous, aggregated
          analytics described above. We also use the technical data to keep the
          service secure: spotting unusual traffic, preventing abuse, and making
          sure the free browser soccer game stays available when a real
          tournament spikes interest. None of this requires knowing who you are,
          which is why the app has no account and no download — you remain
          anonymous to us while you play. If a feature change would need more
          data than this, we would tell you first and ask for consent, because a
          world cup simulator built on trust should not quietly expand its
          collection. In every case, the purpose is the same: a smoother, fairer
          interactive soccer simulator that respects the people who return to it
          as their favourite online soccer game between matches. We do not use
          your activity to target you elsewhere, and we do not build shadow
          profiles from the rosters you assemble in the football draft simulator.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">5. Data sharing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We do not share personal information with third parties except in
          narrow cases: (a) with service providers who help operate the site —
          for example an analytics or hosting partner — and who are bound to keep
          any data confidential and use it only for that purpose; and (b) where
          required by law, such as a valid legal request, or to protect the
          rights, safety and security of the site and its users. Because the
          soccer simulator stores your draft locally, there is normally nothing
          about your squad to share, and we cannot hand over a tournament you
          built because we never received it. The aggregated, non-identifying
          analytics we do hold may be processed by a measurement provider under
          contract, but it is not sold and not used to identify you. We will not
          transfer your information to a buyer in a way that breaks this policy,
          and if the world cup fantasy game ever changed ownership we would
          notify users and keep commitments at least as protective as these. We
          also will not share data with advertisers, because the football draft
          simulator carries no ad network and no cross-site tracking. In
          practice, the only sharing is the limited, confidential help that keeps
          the free browser soccer game online — and even then, the rosters you
          draft and the cups you win never leave your device. A world cup
          simulator should feel like a private playground, and our data-sharing
          rules are written so the interactive soccer simulator stays that way,
          whether you found it as a soccer draft game, a free soccer simulation
          game, or simply the easiest online soccer game to open on a phone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">6. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not
          knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. Because
          the soccer simulator requires no account and no sign-up, a child can
          open the world cup fantasy game and play without giving us a name,
          email or any other identifier, which keeps the risk low by design. We
          do not ask for age during play, and we do not gate the football draft
          simulator behind a registration wall that would encourage false
          details. If a parent or guardian believes a child under 13 has
          submitted personal information to us through another channel — for
          example an email to the contact page — we will delete it promptly on
          request. The content itself, drawn from World Cup history, is broadly
          suitable for football fans of any age, and many families use the
          interactive soccer simulator as a light, educational way to explore the
          greatest world cup teams together. We still recommend that younger
          players use the free browser soccer game with a parent, both for
          screen-time balance and because the squads are editorial, not official
          records. Should the law in your region set a different age threshold
          for consent, that threshold applies to you, and we will honour it. Our
          aim is simple: a soccer game no download that families can enjoy
          knowing the fantasy soccer draft collects essentially nothing, and an
          online soccer game whose privacy stance is as friendly as its gameplay.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">7. Your choices</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can clear your game data at any time by clearing your browser
          storage for the site, which removes your drafts, squads and saved
          cups, and you can opt out of cookie-based tracking through your browser
          settings or the analytics provider's opt-out tools. Because the soccer
          simulator keeps everything local, clearing storage is a complete
          reset — there is no server copy of your tournament to untangle. You may
          also block or delete individual cookies, enable "Do Not Track" if your
          browser supports it, or use a privacy extension, and the football
          draft simulator will still run because all matches are computed on your
          device. Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights
          under local law — for example to access, correct or delete personal
          data we hold, or to object to certain processing — and you can exercise
          those rights by contacting us through the contact page. We will respond
          within the timeframe the law requires and will not penalise you for
          asking. The world cup fantasy game is built so these choices are easy:
          no account means nothing to deactivate, and no download means nothing
          to uninstall. Whether you came to us as a soccer draft game, a free
          soccer simulation game or an interactive soccer simulator, your control
          over the experience is the same — open the online soccer game, play as
          much as you like, and clear it in seconds when you are done. A
          world cup simulator should hand you the controls, both on the pitch and
          over your own data, and this policy is where we make that promise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We may update this policy from time to time as the soccer simulator
          evolves, and changes will be posted on this page with an updated "Last
          updated" date at the top. If a change is significant — for example if
          we ever added a feature that collected more than the anonymous,
          aggregated analytics described here — we would say so clearly and,
          where the law requires, ask for your consent before it took effect.
          Minor changes, such as clarifying wording or reflecting a new browser
          storage method in the football draft simulator, may be made without
          notice beyond the date stamp. We encourage you to revisit this page
          occasionally, especially if you rely on the world cup fantasy game for
          a class, a community or a regular match-day ritual. The spirit of the
          policy will not change: the free browser soccer game collects as little
          as possible, sells nothing, and keeps your drafts on your device. If
          you disagree with a future update, your remedy is simple — you can stop
          using the site and clear your storage, because there is no account to
          close and no download to remove. We will also keep an archive mindset:
          the interactive soccer simulator should stay trustworthy as it grows,
          whether we add more historical squads, deeper football formations or a
          richer penalty shootout simulator. However you found us — as a soccer
          draft game, a free soccer simulation game, or the easiest online soccer
          game to open between matches — this policy is the place we explain our
          side of the bargain, and the "Last updated" line is the honest marker
          of when that explanation last changed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">9. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Questions about this policy, or about how the soccer simulator
          handles your data? We are happy to help. The fastest route is the
          contact page, where you can write to us about anything from a cookie
          setting to a feature idea for the football draft simulator. Because the
          world cup fantasy game stores your drafts locally, most "can you delete
          my data" questions are answered by clearing your browser storage — but
          if you want us to address anything we do hold, such as analytics
          preferences, we will action it promptly. We also welcome notes from
          parents, teachers and community organisers who use the free browser
          soccer game as a classroom or match-day tool and want reassurance about
          what stays on device. You can reach us whether you found the app as a
          soccer draft game, a free soccer simulation game or an interactive
          soccer simulator, and we read every message even when the inbox is busy
          around a real tournament. Privacy is not a one-time checkbox for a
          world cup simulator; it is an ongoing promise, and the contact page is
          where that promise stays accountable. If something in this policy is
          unclear, tell us in plain words and we will do our best to explain it
          plainly back. <a class="text-mint underline" href="/contact">Contact us</a>
          and help keep the online soccer game as respectful of your data as it
          is free to play.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</main></Layout>
